    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `timezone` field is a response-time derived value on the owner, following the same pattern as the existing `locality`, `contactPreference`, etc.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` property to the owner response schema (right after `locality`). `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - A fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`).\n   - `getTimezone()`, which derives the IANA name from `getLocality()` (the owner's region), returning `null` for an unknown region.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` \u2014 which creates a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) and asserts `$.locality == \"NSW\"` and `$.timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` \u2014 passes.\n\nNote: this is a plain `@RestController`-derived DTO/model change (region\u2192timezone lookup on the entity), so no new OfficeFloor endpoint pipeline was needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwner`/`OwnerMapper` path picks up the new derived getter automatically.",
