    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the codebase's established pattern for derived, response-time Owner fields.\n\n- The `REGION_TIMEZONE` table sits with its siblings `CITY_REGION` and `REGION_POSTCODES`, using the same `Map.of` shape and the same \"Fixed ... table used to derive {@link ...}\" javadoc convention.\n- `getTimezone()` is placed right after `getLocality()` and alongside `getContactPreference()`/`getCheckDigit()`, matching the existing family of one-line derived getters (\"derived at response time ... Not persisted\"). Logic lives in the right unit \u2014 the `Owner` model, not a new catch-all helper.\n- Keying the lookup on `getLocality()` is the natural fit: that accessor returns the region prefix (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`), so no duplicate region-derivation logic is introduced; it reuses the existing accessor rather than re-parsing `customerCode`.\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` property mirrors the adjacent `readOnly` derived fields (title/description/example/`readOnly: true`), consistent with the schema's existing entries.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer of this file would find it a natural addition.",
